      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06055_kanshasuru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{先生|せんせい}に{感謝|かんしゃ}の{気持|きも}ちを{伝|つた}えたい。",
      "english": "I want to convey my gratitude to my teacher.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06055_kanshasuru_ex5",
      "japanese": "{毎日|まいにち}{健康|けんこう}でいられることに{感謝|かんしゃ}しなければならない。",
      "english": "We should be grateful for being healthy every day.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Pattern: Xに{感謝|かんしゃ}する (be grateful to X) / Xに{感謝|かんしゃ}する (thank X for Y).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates ongoing state of gratitude. {感謝|かんしゃ}している = 'am grateful.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{心|こころ}から{感謝|かんしゃ}する (thank from the bottom of one's heart)\n・{深|ふか}く{感謝|かんしゃ}する (deeply appreciate)\n・{感謝|かんしゃ}の{気持|きも}ちを{伝|つた}える (convey one's gratitude)\n\nREGISTER: More formal than ありがとう. Often used in business, speeches, and written communication.\n\nRELATED: The noun {感謝|かんしゃ} (gratitude) is commonly used on its own.",
